      "suggestedVersionCode": "78",
      "description": "A bank SMS is already a statement line. Ours reads the ones an Indian bank or UPI app sends, turns them into transactions, and keeps two phones in one household agreeing about them.\n\n* Parses debits, credits, card purchases, card bills and self-transfers out of SMS \u2014 no typing, no CSV, no bank login.\n* One budget over one household, not one per person: spending is measured against everything the household spent, whoever spent it.\n* Three kinds of account, because a balance means three different things. Money in a current account is available; money on a credit card is owed; money in an FD, an RD or a PPF is held. Only the first is safe to spend, and the app never quietly adds the other two to it.\n* Unknown is never zero. An account nobody has quoted a balance for is counted and reported as unknown, not summed as \u20b90.\n* Syncs between phones over a Google Sheet the household owns, or directly over Bluetooth. There is no server and no account.\n\nBuilt for one household and sideloaded to two phones with real money in them, so it is opinionated about Indian bank message formats and makes no attempt to be a general-purpose tracker.",
      "issueTracker": "https://github.com/manuelfc1991/expense-tracker/issues",
      "license": "GPL-3.0-only",
      "name": "Ours",
      "sourceCode": "https://github.com/manuelfc1991/expense-tracker",
      "summary": "Reads bank SMS into a shared household ledger",
      "added": 1786266565000,
      "packageName": "com.manuel.ours",
      "lastUpdated": 1786294094000,
      "localized": {
        "en-US": {
          "icon": "icon_FEGtXdyPgmdULmqorXWJhBQfxZcTH8qEUPSZ1VXf24M=.png",
          "phoneScreenshots": [
            "01-home.png",
            "02-activity.png",
            "03-month.png",
            "04-accounts.png",
            "05-put-aside.png",
            "06-sort.png"
          ],
          "whatsNew": "Spending on a credit card was being subtracted from what the app said you owed, rather than added to it. Both a purchase and a bill payment arrive from the bank as a debit, and only the purchase was going the wrong way \u2014 so the more a card was used, the smaller its outstanding looked.\n\nCard rows now say where their figure came from, the same way bank accounts already did: amber \"you said\" when somebody typed it, and a line for anything the app has applied since. A card's outstanding is often the"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
